{
  "video": {
    "id": "jOBBwI4CYjM",
    "title": "Direction Fields | MIT 18.03SC Differential Equations, Fall 2011",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jOBBwI4CYjM",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 669,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 244,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 8.51,
      "end": 8.52,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Hi everyone. Welcome back. So today, I'd"
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 8.52,
      "end": 9.87,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "like to tackle a problem on direction"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 9.88,
      "end": 11.11,
      "duration": 1.23,
      "text": "fields."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 11.12,
      "end": 13.67,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "So given a differential equation y prime"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 13.68,
      "end": 15.63,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "equals negative y divided by x squared"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 15.64,
      "end": 17.15,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "plus y squared,"
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 17.16,
      "end": 18.51,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "we're asked to first sketch the"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 18.52,
      "end": 20.03,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "direction field,"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 20.04,
      "end": 21.55,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "and then secondly,"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 21.56,
      "end": 23.83,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "given the curve that goes through y zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 23.84,
      "end": 26.15,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "equals one, we're asked"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 26.16,
      "end": 28.95,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "several questions about it. Why is y of"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 28.96,
      "end": 30.79,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "x greater than zero for x greater than"
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 30.8,
      "end": 31.71,
      "duration": 0.91,
      "text": "zero?"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 31.72,
      "end": 33.95,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "And then why is y of x decreasing for x"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 33.96,
      "end": 35.59,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "greater than zero? So let you think"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 35.6,
      "end": 37.03,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "about this for a moment and I'll get"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 37.04,
      "end": 47.27,
      "duration": 10.23,
      "text": "back."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 49.55,
      "end": 49.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Hi everyone. Welcome back."
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 49.56,
      "end": 50.47,
      "duration": 0.91,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 50.48,
      "end": 52.63,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "So to start off this problem, we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 52.64,
      "end": 54.75,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "asked to sketch the direction field."
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 54.76,
      "end": 56.39,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "Now, when asked to sketch a direction"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 56.4,
      "end": 58.19,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "field, the first thing to do is to look"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 58.2,
      "end": 64.869,
      "duration": 6.669,
      "text": "at a couple isoclines."
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 66.99,
      "end": 67.0,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So what is an isocline?"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 67.0,
      "end": 70.67,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "Well, it's a curve"
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 72.67,
      "end": 72.68,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "where the derivative y prime is equal to"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 72.68,
      "end": 73.83,
      "duration": 1.15,
      "text": "m,"
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 73.84,
      "end": 79.19,
      "duration": 5.35,
      "text": "which is some constant."
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 80.87,
      "end": 80.88,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So what are the isoclines for this"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 80.88,
      "end": 85.03,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "differential equation?"
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 87.99,
      "end": 88.0,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Well, it would be minus y"
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 88.0,
      "end": 92.87,
      "duration": 4.87,
      "text": "divided by x squared plus y squared"
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 94.55,
      "end": 94.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "equals m."
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 94.56,
      "end": 97.03,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "Now, of particular interest,"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 97.04,
      "end": 99.35,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "there's a very special isocline which is"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 99.36,
      "end": 101.83,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "usually the easiest"
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 101.84,
      "end": 105.19,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "to plot,"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 107.03,
      "end": 107.04,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "and that's a nullcline. And this is just"
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 107.04,
      "end": 111.07,
      "duration": 4.03,
      "text": "a special case where m is equal to zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 113.55,
      "end": 113.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So what's the nullcline for this ODE?"
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 113.56,
      "end": 115.31,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "Well, when m is equal to zero, the only"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 115.32,
      "end": 117.03,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "way that"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 117.04,
      "end": 124.07,
      "duration": 7.03,
      "text": "y prime can be zero is when y is zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 126.47,
      "end": 126.48,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay, so the nullcline for this ODE is y"
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 126.48,
      "end": 128.63,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "equals zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 128.64,
      "end": 132.27,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "Now, for more general isoclines,"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 132.28,
      "end": 134.27,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "we're left with this relation between x"
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 134.28,
      "end": 135.35,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "and y."
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 135.36,
      "end": 137.67,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "And we can massage this expression to"
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 137.68,
      "end": 147.35,
      "duration": 9.67,
      "text": "see exactly what the isoclines are."
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 149.03,
      "end": 149.04,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So specifically, I'm going to multiply"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 149.04,
      "end": 150.95,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "through by x squared plus y squared, and"
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 150.96,
      "end": 153.71,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "I'm going to divide by m."
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 153.72,
      "end": 155.39,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "And we see that we have a quadratic in x"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 155.4,
      "end": 157.83,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "and y, and we have one linear term."
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 157.84,
      "end": 159.71,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "So whenever we have a relation like"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 159.72,
      "end": 161.19,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "this, and we want to understand what it"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 161.2,
      "end": 162.27,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "looks like,"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 162.28,
      "end": 163.35,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "typically the approach is just to"
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 163.36,
      "end": 165.43,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "complete the square."
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 165.44,
      "end": 168.31,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "So I'm going to bring the one over m y"
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 168.32,
      "end": 179.95,
      "duration": 11.63,
      "text": "to the other side of the equation."
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 181.03,
      "end": 181.04,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And I'm going to combine it with y"
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 181.04,
      "end": 192.71,
      "duration": 11.67,
      "text": "squared to complete the square."
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 198.91,
      "end": 198.92,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "we obtain the following equation,"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 198.92,
      "end": 200.99,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "and we recognize this equation as the"
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 201.0,
      "end": 208.63,
      "duration": 7.63,
      "text": "equation for a circle."
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 210.23,
      "end": 210.24,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Specifically, it's a circle that's"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 210.24,
      "end": 211.95,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "centered at"
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 211.96,
      "end": 214.39,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "x is equal to zero,"
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 214.4,
      "end": 216.19,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "and y is equal to negative one over two"
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 216.2,
      "end": 220.03,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "text": "m."
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 223.11,
      "end": 223.12,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And in addition,"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 223.12,
      "end": 225.23,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "the circle has a radius"
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 225.24,
      "end": 227.11,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "r squared is equal to one over four m"
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 227.12,
      "end": 230.35,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "squared,"
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 232.55,
      "end": 232.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "which means its radius is one over two"
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 232.56,
      "end": 237.47,
      "duration": 4.91,
      "text": "times the absolute value of m."
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 239.19,
      "end": 239.2,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay, so why don't we take a look and"
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 239.2,
      "end": 253.27,
      "duration": 14.07,
      "text": "plot a couple isoclines."
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 255.75,
      "end": 255.76,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay, so as I mentioned before,"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 255.76,
      "end": 257.39,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "typically the first isocline that we"
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 257.4,
      "end": 258.91,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "should plot is the nullcline, which is m"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 258.92,
      "end": 260.349,
      "duration": 1.429,
      "text": "is equal to zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 260.359,
      "end": 262.31,
      "duration": 1.951,
      "text": "And we know that this is y is equal to"
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 262.32,
      "end": 263.71,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 263.72,
      "end": 265.87,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "So all along the line y is equal to"
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 265.88,
      "end": 268.39,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "zero, I'm just going to draw dashes"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 268.4,
      "end": 271.67,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "that correspond to a slope"
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 271.68,
      "end": 274.95,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "of y is equal to zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 276.59,
      "end": 276.6,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "For the other isoclines, we just have to"
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 276.6,
      "end": 278.11,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "pick some values of m and start"
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 278.12,
      "end": 279.71,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "plotting."
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 279.72,
      "end": 281.75,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "So I'll take the value m is equal to"
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 281.76,
      "end": 283.11,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "negative one."
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 283.12,
      "end": 284.63,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "And when m is equal to negative one, we"
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 284.64,
      "end": 286.07,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "have a circle which is centered at zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 286.08,
      "end": 298.87,
      "duration": 12.79,
      "text": "and one half with radius one half."
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 304.83,
      "end": 304.84,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Here's one."
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 304.84,
      "end": 307.55,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "And at every point along this circle,"
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 307.56,
      "end": 312.95,
      "duration": 5.39,
      "text": "we just draw a little slope"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 318.47,
      "end": 318.48,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So at every point along this curve, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 318.48,
      "end": 321.19,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "solution has slope negative one."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 321.2,
      "end": 323.47,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "Now, in addition, we can also"
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 323.48,
      "end": 330.47,
      "duration": 6.99,
      "text": "get another circle,"
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 337.67,
      "end": 337.68,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And this corresponds to the isocline of"
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 337.68,
      "end": 343.43,
      "duration": 5.75,
      "text": "m is equal to plus one."
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 346.79,
      "end": 346.8,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And every point on this circle"
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 346.8,
      "end": 350.91,
      "duration": 4.11,
      "text": "has slope plus one."
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 353.15,
      "end": 353.16,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Those should all be the same."
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 353.16,
      "end": 354.27,
      "duration": 1.11,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 354.28,
      "end": 355.59,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "And now we can pick some other values of"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 355.6,
      "end": 359.43,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "text": "m. So for example, m is equal to two."
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 359.44,
      "end": 361.59,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "If m is equal to two,"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 361.6,
      "end": 363.11,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "then we have a circle which is centered"
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 363.12,
      "end": 365.07,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "at negative one fourth and radius one"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 365.08,
      "end": 370.51,
      "duration": 5.43,
      "text": "fourth."
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 373.67,
      "end": 373.68,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So it might look something like this."
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 373.68,
      "end": 375.43,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "And m is equal to negative two might"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 375.44,
      "end": 376.99,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "look something like this."
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 377.0,
      "end": 380.51,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "So this is m is equal to negative two."
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 380.52,
      "end": 384.55,
      "duration": 4.03,
      "text": "This is m is equal to two."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 386.15,
      "end": 386.16,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And the slope on this curve is going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 386.16,
      "end": 388.11,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "be steeper."
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 388.12,
      "end": 395.43,
      "duration": 7.31,
      "text": "It's going to be negative two."
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 398.43,
      "end": 398.44,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And the same goes for this circle."
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 398.44,
      "end": 401.31,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "And then lastly, I can draw a sketch of"
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 401.32,
      "end": 405.47,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "m is equal to three hat three quarters,"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 412.87,
      "end": 412.88,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Sorry, m is equal to negative three"
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 412.88,
      "end": 414.39,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "quarters."
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 414.4,
      "end": 417.75,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "And that would have a slightly"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 424.83,
      "end": 424.84,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay, so notice how the collection of"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 424.84,
      "end": 427.71,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "isoclines are a family of circles"
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 427.72,
      "end": 430.03,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "that all are tangent to the origin. And"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 430.04,
      "end": 431.55,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "in fact, if we think about it, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 431.56,
      "end": 433.75,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "nullcline, the m equals zero line,"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 433.76,
      "end": 436.63,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "is actually in some sense a limit circle"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 436.64,
      "end": 438.03,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "where we take the radius and the center"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 438.04,
      "end": 440.55,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "going to infinity. So as the circles"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 440.56,
      "end": 442.67,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "become larger and larger, they tend to"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 442.68,
      "end": 446.59,
      "duration": 3.91,
      "text": "approach this line y equals zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 446.6,
      "end": 449.75,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "Okay, so this this concludes part one."
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 449.76,
      "end": 452.43,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "So for part two, we're now asked"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 452.44,
      "end": 453.99,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "several questions about the the curve"
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 454.0,
      "end": 455.47,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "which goes through y zero is equal to"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 455.48,
      "end": 457.39,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "one."
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 457.4,
      "end": 459.35,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "So I'll just sketch what this solution"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 459.36,
      "end": 460.91,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "curve might look like,"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 460.92,
      "end": 462.15,
      "duration": 1.23,
      "text": "and"
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 462.16,
      "end": 464.83,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "it's going to start off at a slope"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 464.84,
      "end": 467.11,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "of one of negative one, and then it's"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 467.12,
      "end": 468.43,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "going to hit these circles which have a"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 468.44,
      "end": 471.83,
      "duration": 3.39,
      "text": "steeper slope."
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 473.19,
      "end": 473.2,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And then eventually, it's it's going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 473.2,
      "end": 474.59,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "go through the circles with a steeper"
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 474.6,
      "end": 476.11,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "slope and come back to the circle that"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 476.12,
      "end": 477.23,
      "duration": 1.11,
      "text": "has slope"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 477.24,
      "end": 479.71,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "negative one, and eventually"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 479.72,
      "end": 482.59,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "decay outwards."
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 482.6,
      "end": 484.23,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "So this is what the solution curve might"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 484.24,
      "end": 486.11,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "look like. I'm just sketching this"
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 486.12,
      "end": 487.07,
      "duration": 0.95,
      "text": "uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 487.08,
      "end": 489.71,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "to set up parts uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 489.72,
      "end": 491.75,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "two A and two B here."
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 491.76,
      "end": 494.91,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "Okay, so why is y of x"
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 494.92,
      "end": 496.51,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "uh always bigger than"
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 496.52,
      "end": 499.55,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "zero for x greater than zero?"
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 499.56,
      "end": 503.79,
      "duration": 4.23,
      "text": "Well, we see that this solution curve"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 506.55,
      "end": 506.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "uh stays in the upper half plane,"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 506.56,
      "end": 513.75,
      "duration": 7.19,
      "text": "and we note that y is equal to zero,"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 515.67,
      "end": 515.68,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "which is the nullcline, is actually a"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 515.68,
      "end": 517.709,
      "duration": 2.029,
      "text": "very special curve. Not only is it the"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 517.719,
      "end": 519.79,
      "duration": 2.071,
      "text": "nullcline, but it is it's actually a"
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 519.8,
      "end": 521.95,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "solution to the differential equation."
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 521.96,
      "end": 523.27,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "So if we look back at the differential"
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 523.28,
      "end": 524.59,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "equation,"
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 524.6,
      "end": 525.87,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "we see that"
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 525.88,
      "end": 528.67,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "y is equal to zero has zero derivative,"
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 528.68,
      "end": 529.51,
      "duration": 0.83,
      "text": "and the right hand side of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 529.52,
      "end": 531.71,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "differential equation is also zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 531.72,
      "end": 533.91,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "So this is not only a nullcline, but"
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 533.92,
      "end": 535.11,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "it's a solution to the differential"
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 535.12,
      "end": 536.15,
      "duration": 1.03,
      "text": "equation."
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 536.16,
      "end": 538.51,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "Note that this is extremely special."
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 538.52,
      "end": 540.99,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "In in no way does every nullcline have"
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 541.0,
      "end": 542.43,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "to be a solution to a differential"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 542.44,
      "end": 544.35,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "equation, but in this case, we get"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 544.36,
      "end": 546.55,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "lucky."
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 546.56,
      "end": 548.43,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "Now, we know from the theory of ODEs"
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 548.44,
      "end": 550.71,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "that solution curves can't cross."
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 550.72,
      "end": 552.15,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "So a solution curve that starts in the"
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 552.16,
      "end": 553.79,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "upper half plane"
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 553.8,
      "end": 556.03,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "can't cross another solution, which in"
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 556.04,
      "end": 558.63,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "this case is the y equals zero curve."
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 558.64,
      "end": 560.35,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "Hence, it must be bounded in the upper"
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 560.36,
      "end": 563.35,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "half plane for all x bigger than zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 563.36,
      "end": 564.87,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 564.88,
      "end": 566.83,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "The second part, why is y of x"
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 566.84,
      "end": 569.35,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "decreasing for x greater than zero?"
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 569.36,
      "end": 571.51,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "Well, what we have to look at, so I'll"
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 571.52,
      "end": 576.51,
      "duration": 4.99,
      "text": "just write in here part two."
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 579.75,
      "end": 579.76,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "We have to look at the sign of y prime."
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 579.76,
      "end": 582.95,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "Now, y prime is equal to negative y"
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 582.96,
      "end": 586.51,
      "duration": 3.55,
      "text": "divided by x squared plus y squared."
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 586.52,
      "end": 588.75,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "So as I've just argued, a solution that"
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 588.76,
      "end": 590.59,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "starts in the upper half plane"
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 590.6,
      "end": 591.83,
      "duration": 1.23,
      "text": "and goes through the point y of zero is"
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 591.84,
      "end": 593.55,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "equal to one, stays in the upper half"
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 593.56,
      "end": 596.55,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "plane for all x bigger than zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 596.56,
      "end": 597.91,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "What this means is that the solution"
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 597.92,
      "end": 599.11,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "curve"
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 599.12,
      "end": 601.51,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "has Y bigger than zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 601.52,
      "end": 603.55,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "for all X bigger than zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 603.56,
      "end": 606.87,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "So, that means the numerator"
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 606.88,
      "end": 610.43,
      "duration": 3.55,
      "text": "is always positive."
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 612.71,
      "end": 612.72,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "The denominator"
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 612.72,
      "end": 615.11,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "is also always positive."
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 615.12,
      "end": 616.83,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "So, we have negative a positive number"
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 616.84,
      "end": 618.75,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "divided by a positive number."
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 618.76,
      "end": 620.23,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "And so, this quantity"
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 620.24,
      "end": 623.15,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "is always going to be less than zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 623.16,
      "end": 624.11,
      "duration": 0.95,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 624.12,
      "end": 626.55,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "So, for X bigger than zero, Y prime is"
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 626.56,
      "end": 628.47,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "always going to be less than zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 628.48,
      "end": 630.03,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "Hence, the solution that starts at Y of"
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 630.04,
      "end": 631.51,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "zero is equal to one is going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 228,
      "start": 631.52,
      "end": 633.67,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "monotonically decay to to Y is equal to"
    },
    {
      "index": 229,
      "start": 633.68,
      "end": 635.03,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 230,
      "start": 635.04,
      "end": 637.75,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "Okay. So, this concludes the problem."
    },
    {
      "index": 231,
      "start": 637.76,
      "end": 639.31,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "Now, just to recap,"
    },
    {
      "index": 232,
      "start": 639.32,
      "end": 641.63,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "we were given an ODE. The The standard"
    },
    {
      "index": 233,
      "start": 641.64,
      "end": 643.75,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "approach uh when sketching direction"
    },
    {
      "index": 234,
      "start": 643.76,
      "end": 646.19,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "fields is to pick a few nullclines or to"
    },
    {
      "index": 235,
      "start": 646.2,
      "end": 648.51,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "pick a few isoclines uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 236,
      "start": 648.52,
      "end": 650.95,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "and specifically pick the nullcline,"
    },
    {
      "index": 237,
      "start": 650.96,
      "end": 653.47,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "sketch the isoclines,"
    },
    {
      "index": 238,
      "start": 653.48,
      "end": 655.87,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "and then if you're asked to uh plot any"
    },
    {
      "index": 239,
      "start": 655.88,
      "end": 657.47,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "integral curves or solutions to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 240,
      "start": 657.48,
      "end": 659.51,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "differential equation, you just simply"
    },
    {
      "index": 241,
      "start": 659.52,
      "end": 661.47,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "connect the dots."
    },
    {
      "index": 242,
      "start": 661.48,
      "end": 663.67,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "Okay, so I'd like to conclude here,"
    },
    {
      "index": 243,
      "start": 663.68,
      "end": 666.64,
      "duration": 2.96,
      "text": "and I'll see you next time."
    }
  ],
